{
 "_doc": "Set, boss (GAME_DESIGN.md: The Two Lands bosses; art 10/31/2026). Built by tools/art/build_boss_set.py; rules in docs/ART_RULES.md. As Egyptian temple reliefs and papyri show him (for example at Karnak and Abydos): a man's body with the head of the 'Set animal', with its curved muzzle and tall ears with squared tips, a striped wig, a broad beaded collar, a pleated linen kilt (shendyt) to the knee with a gold belt, and the was-sceptre, a staff topped with the Set animal's head and forked at the foot. Lord of the desert and storms (The Contendings of Horus and Set; Plutarch, On Isis and Osiris, which also gives him red colouring). Skin in the red-brown that Egyptian painting gives men.",
